<title>SWEDEN: Securitas says Q1 profit rises 1.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Securitas says Q1 profit rises 1.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish security company Securitas on Tuesday posted these earnings for the first three months of the year, ending on March 31.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit			   123.5  vs   121.5</p>
<p> Sales				    2,421.7  vs 2,124.9</p>
<p> Earnings per share (crowns)*	 1.22   vs 1.21</p>
<p> Production costs		     1,951.9  vs 1,707.6</p>
<p> Administration costs		   310.4  vs   260.9</p>
<p> Amortization of goodwill		27.0  vs    25.0</p>
<p>Operating profit after  amortization			     132.4  vs   131.4</p>
<p> Net financial items	   CHARGE   8.9  vs     9.9 CHARGE</p>
<p> Taxes paid				  25.4  vs    24.6</p>
<p> Deferred taxes			     5.9  vs     6.6</p>
<p> Minorities			CREDIT   0.9  vs     0.1 CHARGE</p>
<p> Net income				  93.1  vs    90.2</p>
<p>*NOTE -- Earnings per share after 28 percent standard taxes.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1017</p>
</text>
